WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:06.760 --> 00:00:08.920
Life on earth depends
on a Goldilocks climate

00:00:08.920 --> 00:00:11.930
- not too hot and not too cold.

00:00:11.930 --> 00:00:13.900
Humankind is changing that.

00:00:13.900 --> 00:00:17.740
Industrialisation has raised
temperatures around 1 degree.

00:00:17.740 --> 00:00:20.220
Experts think a further
rise of another degree

00:00:20.220 --> 00:00:25.150
is possible by 2052, even
after big emissions cuts.

00:00:25.150 --> 00:00:27.220
Crops will be more
likely to fail,

00:00:27.220 --> 00:00:30.220
displacing human populations.

00:00:30.220 --> 00:00:32.740
In Paris in 2015,
industrialised nations

00:00:32.740 --> 00:00:35.650
agreed they would limit global
warming to less than 2 degrees

00:00:35.650 --> 00:00:39.370
above pre-industrial levels,
but there has been more hot air

00:00:39.370 --> 00:00:40.630
than action.

00:00:40.630 --> 00:00:44.470
Nations cannot agree how much
each should cut emissions.

00:00:44.470 --> 00:00:47.110
Rising populism has
fostered scepticism

00:00:47.110 --> 00:00:49.180
about global warming.

00:00:49.180 --> 00:00:51.640
Under Donald Trump,
the US has threatened

00:00:51.640 --> 00:00:54.100
to withdraw from
the Paris accord.

00:00:54.100 --> 00:00:57.250
They have a collective
action problem.

00:00:57.250 --> 00:01:00.340
Everyone would benefit from
cutting emissions, eventually.

00:01:00.340 --> 00:01:03.010
No one wants to be
the prime mover.

00:01:03.010 --> 00:01:04.910
So there is no progress.

00:01:04.910 --> 00:01:07.180
The reason is that the
costs of global warming

00:01:07.180 --> 00:01:10.780
remain an externality
for most individuals.

00:01:10.780 --> 00:01:13.450
There is no immediate
benefit in reducing them.

00:01:13.450 --> 00:01:16.630
As a result, impacts
are an externality

00:01:16.630 --> 00:01:19.690
to most politicians,
too, except when

00:01:19.690 --> 00:01:21.970
protesters from
Extinction Rebellion

00:01:21.970 --> 00:01:25.490
disrupt the traffic, as
they did recently in London.

00:01:25.490 --> 00:01:27.010
They are preoccupied
with getting

00:01:27.010 --> 00:01:29.240
elected every few years.

00:01:29.240 --> 00:01:33.100
It is, as they sometimes
say in business, NMP,

00:01:33.100 --> 00:01:35.470
or next management's problem.

00:01:35.470 --> 00:01:37.900
By the same logic as
temperatures rise,

00:01:37.900 --> 00:01:40.810
people will start
bearing direct costs.

00:01:40.810 --> 00:01:43.210
For example, some populous
parts of the world

00:01:43.210 --> 00:01:45.690
will become too hot to
inhabit in the summer

00:01:45.690 --> 00:01:47.740
or to visit as tourists.

00:01:47.740 --> 00:01:50.530
The facts such as these will
create an electoral incentive

00:01:50.530 --> 00:01:52.040
to slash emissions.

00:01:52.040 --> 00:01:54.550
Then nations will
start taking action.

00:01:54.550 --> 00:01:56.710
Squabbling will continue.

00:01:56.710 --> 00:02:00.040
One flashpoint will be
output of polluting coal.

00:02:00.040 --> 00:02:05.200
This is expected to peak at well
over 8bn metric tonnes in 2030.

00:02:05.200 --> 00:02:08.500
Many in China and India see
western demands for production

00:02:08.500 --> 00:02:10.660
cuts as self-serving.

00:02:10.660 --> 00:02:13.740
Even within developed nations
there will be conflicts.

00:02:13.740 --> 00:02:16.720
US researchers have predicted
hefty economic damage

00:02:16.720 --> 00:02:19.510
to Texas and Florida
later this century,

00:02:19.510 --> 00:02:22.000
coupled with more modest
benefits for the states

00:02:22.000 --> 00:02:24.070
of Washington and Oregon.

00:02:24.070 --> 00:02:27.040
What will the consequences
be for investors?

00:02:27.040 --> 00:02:30.010
The value of big oil companies,
such as Royal Dutch Shell,

00:02:30.010 --> 00:02:31.330
would fall.

00:02:31.330 --> 00:02:34.360
If reserves cannot be
exploited fully they need to be

00:02:34.360 --> 00:02:36.280
discounted heavily.

00:02:36.280 --> 00:02:39.580
The value of renewables
groups, like Denmark's Orsted,

00:02:39.580 --> 00:02:42.700
would go up reflecting
a growing market.

00:02:42.700 --> 00:02:45.670
Their technologies would depend
less and less on subsidies

00:02:45.670 --> 00:02:47.230
to make profits.

00:02:47.230 --> 00:02:49.450
Nuclear generation
would make a resurgence

00:02:49.450 --> 00:02:52.660
as a supplier of
baseload electricity.

00:02:52.660 --> 00:02:54.850
That would bolster
the price of uranium,

00:02:54.850 --> 00:02:58.180
which has been depressed
since the Fukushima disaster.

00:02:58.180 --> 00:03:00.970
Extreme weather would
become more common.

00:03:00.970 --> 00:03:03.370
That would make farming
investment riskier,

00:03:03.370 --> 00:03:06.820
but agricultural commodities
trading more lucrative.

00:03:06.820 --> 00:03:08.650
Demand for catastrophe
insurance would

00:03:08.650 --> 00:03:12.470
continue to rise sharply,
bolstering Lloyd's of London

00:03:12.470 --> 00:03:15.480
and the market for
catastrophe bonds.

00:03:15.480 --> 00:03:18.120
Some competing companies
appear more committed

00:03:18.120 --> 00:03:21.570
to a low-carbon economy
than competing nations.

00:03:21.570 --> 00:03:24.510
JPMorgan estimates
three-fifths of car sales

00:03:24.510 --> 00:03:28.500
would be hybrids or
fully electric by 2030.

00:03:28.500 --> 00:03:32.550
That compares with
2 per cent in 2015.

00:03:32.550 --> 00:03:37.020
Lex believes big traditional
carmakers, such as VW and GM,

00:03:37.020 --> 00:03:39.060
will succeed in
switching wholesale

00:03:39.060 --> 00:03:41.730
into electric vehicle output.

00:03:41.730 --> 00:03:45.030
They understand mass
production, after all.

00:03:45.030 --> 00:03:48.780
That will leave Tesla where it
is now, as a niche business,

00:03:48.780 --> 00:03:50.550
if it is not bought out.

00:03:50.550 --> 00:03:54.120
Another interesting niche will
be hydrogen fuel cell vehicles.

00:03:54.120 --> 00:03:56.460
Toyota has made a
side bet these will be

00:03:56.460 --> 00:03:58.560
needed for hauling heavy loads.

00:03:58.560 --> 00:03:59.700
The reason?

00:03:59.700 --> 00:04:02.280
Growth in the weight-to-power
ratio of batteries

00:04:02.280 --> 00:04:03.870
has been linear.

00:04:03.870 --> 00:04:05.490
Exponential growth
would be needed

00:04:05.490 --> 00:04:10.320
for battery-powered vehicles to
become universal, experts say.

00:04:10.320 --> 00:04:13.380
Businesses will need to make a
lot of other intelligent bets

00:04:13.380 --> 00:04:15.960
to build the low-carbon economy.

00:04:15.960 --> 00:04:18.300
Governments will belatedly
impose the incentives

00:04:18.300 --> 00:04:20.079
and penalties needed.

00:04:20.079 --> 00:04:22.200
The one certainty
of climate change

00:04:22.200 --> 00:04:26.450
is that business as usual
will not be an option.

